scene.fog = new THREE.Fog(0x060a18, 400, 3500);
const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(65, innerWidth/innerHeight, 1, 20000);
```
Wait, `renderer.setPixelRatio` after setSize is fine.

Hmm but removing logarithmicDepthBuffer: ECEF coordinates are huge (6.3e6). Float32 precision at 6.3e6 magnitude is ~0.5m. The positions are stored as floats — model positions relative to their tile transform. 3d-tiles applies cachedTransform per tile so world coords are ECEF. Float32 rounding of ~0.4m might make buildings jitter when moving? Objects are static so fine.

Depth buffer precision: with near=1, far=20000. 24-bit depth: precision at distance d ≈ d²/(near * 2^24)... For d=300m: 90000/(1*16.7M)=0.0054m = 5mm. Fine. For d=3000m: 9e6/1.67e7=0.54m. Slight z-fighting at 3km but fog hides it (fog far 3500). OK.

So removing log depth buffer is acceptable. 

